    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Kotlin "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "extensions"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://kotlinlang.org/docs/extensions.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " provide the ability to extend existing classes with additional functionality. The Spring Framework Kotlin APIs use these extensions to add new Kotlin-specific conveniences to existing Spring APIs."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Spring Framework KDoc API"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/kdoc-api/"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " lists and documents all available Kotlin extensions and DSLs."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Keep in mind that Kotlin extensions need to be imported to be used. This means, for example, that the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "GenericApplicationContext.registerBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " Kotlin extension is available only if "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "org.springframework.context.support.registerBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is imported. That said, similar to static imports, an IDE should automatically suggest the import in most cases."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "For example, "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Kotlin reified type parameters"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://kotlinlang.org/docs/inline-functions.html#reified-type-parameters"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " provide a workaround for JVM "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "generics type erasure"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/java/generics/erasure.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", and the Spring Framework provides some extensions to take advantage of this feature. This allows for a better Kotlin API "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "RestTemplate"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", for the new "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " from Spring WebFlux, and for various other APIs."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Other libraries, such as Reactor and Spring Data, also provide Kotlin extensions for their APIs, thus giving a better Kotlin development experience overall."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To retrieve a list of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "User"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " objects in Java, you would normally write the following:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Flux<User> users  = client.get().retrieve().bodyToFlux(User.class)"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "With Kotlin and the Spring Framework extensions, you can instead write the following:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "val users = client.get().retrieve().bodyToFlux<User>()\n// or (both are equivalent)\nval users : Flux<User> = client.get().retrieve().bodyToFlux()"
          }
        ],
        "language": "kotlin",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "As in Java, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "users"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " in Kotlin is strongly typed, but Kotlin’s clever type inference allows for shorter syntax."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Extensions"
      }
    ]
  }
}
